.TH TEE 1
.SH NAME
tee \- pipe fitting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tee
[
.B \-a
]
.I file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tee
transcribes the standard input to the standard
output and makes copies in the
.IR files .
Each file is created, or truncated if it exists.
The option
.B \-a
appends the output to the
.I files
rather than rewriting them.
It is recognised only as the first argument.
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/tee/main.odin
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The exit status is empty, or
.B "can't open"
when a file could not be opened.
The input is still copied to the files that could.
.SH BUGS
An error writing to a file is not reported.
